My character has successfully descended to the bottom of the Gnomish
mines.  It seems that the luck stone there is no longer guaranteed?  At
first sight, the bottom was the old design dating back to NH 3.1.3.  But
there were two more doors to small chambers.  When I went to the usual
place with the luck stone, there was no gray stone - so I was warned. 
In one of the other chambers, I found a gray stone, but I was careful to
kick it first.  Since it hurted ("ouch"), I avoided picking it up.  I am
not sure whether I like the absence of a guaranteed luck stone; it takes
a lot out of the motivation to go down to the bottom of the mines in
spite of possible polymorph traps.  (I liked the addition of Sokoban a
lot, going in the opposite sense - giving you an additional guaranteed
item, though randomly chosen out of two useful ones.)

In fact, my character got lucky with a polymorph trap.  When he stepped
on it, he got the message: "You feel a change coming over you.  You feel
like a new orc!"  Phew.  I already saw my nice +2 cloak of displacement
from the initial inventory torn to pieces.  In addition, my stats went
up.  Strength, dexterity, and constitution all up one point.  Only
afterwards did I realize that with an AC of -10 or -11 (depending on the
rust status of my dwarvish iron helm), I could afford taking off the
cloak until I got back up above level 8.  The dwarvish mithril coat
(even though +1) is replacable (and not my final armour anyway, if I
survive...) and the +5 elven boots won't get destroyed on a polymorph. 
So I did this, but of course a polymorph trap could still destroy the
whole game...  I need magic resistance badly...

Another thing that I learned (actually should have known, but I did not
think sharply enough...) was when I encountered a werewolf who summoned
a bunch of winter wolf cubs, at the bottom of mines.  Their frost blasts
took me down from 71 to 26 hit points quite fast.  My intended life
saver, a wand of digging, would of course not work here.  So I checked
my inventory to see if I could do anything.  Yess!!  I still had this
uncursed scroll of genocide.  Of course, I would have liked to use it on
bigger baddies later (L, for example), but I might not live for later. 
So I read it, was asked what type of monster I would like to genocide,
and typed "winter wolf".  "Wiped out all winter wolves".  But none of
the cubs!  Aren't they winter wolves?  Of course, they are young winter
wolves, but genocide does not work as I thought in that moment.  It does
not erase a single species but a single type of monster.  And I had just
chosen the wrong one.  (Probably the fact also played a role, that
usually I wait until I can bless my scrolls of genocide, and then, you
always erase several types of monsters.)  Well, I survived nonetheless,
because after that each of the cubs fell to my next hit (four of them);
but they brought me down to 17 hp.  Only then did I think of putting
back on my cloak to heal faster.  Another cub came along, which was
disposed of fast.  An ettin mummy stopped my healing for a while around
25 hp, but eventually I was back to 71, and by some experience richer...

